    "lesson_id": "012",
    "trigger_word": "mji",
    "trigger_card_number": 1,
    "title": "LESSON 12: PLACE IS A SUFFIX",
    "header_color": "cyan",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "No 'in', no 'at', no 'to'. Hang -ni on",
          "the end of a noun and it becomes a",
          "place:",
          "",
          "   mji     ->  mjini      in town",
          "   nyumba  ->  nyumbani   at home",
          "   shule   ->  shuleni    at school",
          "   soko    ->  sokoni     at the market",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "One suffix does the work of three",
          "English prepositions — the verb",
          "decides whether you are in, at, or",
          "headed to."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Mjini. Nyumbani. Shuleni. Sokoni."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "Watch it work with verbs you own:",
          "",
          "   Ninakwenda mjini.",
          "   I am going to town.",
          "",
          "   Anakaa nyumbani leo.",
          "   She is staying home today.",
          "",
          "   Wanajifunza shuleni.",
          "   They study at school.",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "Proper names refuse the suffix:",
          "you go to Dodoma, never 'Dodomani'.",
          "Places that are already places",
          "don't need the badge."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Ninakwenda mjini. Anakaa nyumbani leo. Wanajifunza shuleni."
        }
      }
    ]
  },
