          "2": "Amefika. Tumemaliza."
        }
      },
      {
        "page": 2,
        "total_pages": 2,
        "content": [
          "-me- loves states. Where English says",
          "'is', Swahili often says 'has become':",
          "",
          "   Amelala.     He has lain down",
          "                = he is asleep.",
          "",
          "   Imevunjika.  It has broken",
          "                = it is broken.",
          "",
          "Hear them:                         Press 1",
          "",
          "Your helper bado (still, not yet)",
          "is -me-'s natural partner: what is",
          "not yet done stays bado. The full",
          "not-yet machinery arrives with the",
          "negation lessons in Pareto 1."
        ],
        "pronunciation_mappings": {
          "1": "Amelala. Imevunjika."
        }
      }
    ]
